sn1.23:3.1 starts: “Those for whom lust and hatred
sn1.23:3.2 starts: Along with ignorance have been expunged,
sn1.23:3.3 starts: The arahants with taints destroyed:
sn1.23:3.4 starts: For them the tangle is disentangled.
sn1.30:1.1 starts: “Having approached you, we ask a question
sn1.30:1.2 starts: Of the slender hero with antelope calves,
sn1.30:1.3 starts: Greedless, subsisting on little food,
sn1.30:1.4 starts: Wandering alone like a lion or naga,
sn1.30:1.5 starts: Without concern for sensual pleasures:
sn1.30:1.6 starts: How is one released from suffering?”
sn1.32:10.1 starts: “The bad do not emulate the good,
sn1.32:10.2 starts: Who give what is hard to give
sn1.32:10.3 starts: And do deeds hard to do:
sn1.32:10.4 starts: The Dhamma of the good is hard to
